==English==

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|la|dēsīderātum|t=something that is desired}}, neuter nominative singular of {{m|la|dēsīderātus}}, the [[passive voice|passive]] [[past participle]] of the verb {{m|la|[[desidero|dēsīderāre]]|t=to [[desire]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪˌsɪdəˈɹɑːtəm/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|desiderata}}

# Something that is [[wish]]ed for, or considered [[desirable]].
#* '''1907''', ''The Medical Brief'' (volume 35, page 840)
#*: A heavy clay soil is bad for all neuralgics, and the house should be dry, and on a sandy or gravel soil. The '''desideratum''' for all neuralgic affections is perpetual summer {{...}}

